"answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative focused on data analytics, cloud storage optimization, and secure file sharing. It was initially introduced with a kickoff scheduled for June 15th (or July 15th in one update) and led by Sarah Tan or Marcus Cole. The project received a budget approval of $2 million, with an initial phase budget of $500,000 and a separate $15,000 approved for training. The team expanded by adding five members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. Key milestones include the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule, with upcoming phases involving UI enhancements in October and security protocol updates (MFA and encryption) effective January next year. Feedback on the prototype was requested by the end of November, and the project is described as almost complete."
